<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine satellite launch deferred.</title>
<headline>Philippine satellite launch deferred.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mabuhay Philippines Satellite Corp said on Monday the launching of its communications satellite has been postponed to August 14 from August 10.</p>
<p>Mabuhay said in a statement the satellite's manufacturer Space Systems/Loral recommended the deferment after finding out that corrective measures have to be made on the rocket that will launch the satellite.</p>
<p>The Agila II satellite will be the first to be launched by a Filipino-led consortium.</p>
<p>Mabuhay is a consortium led by Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co with a 51 percent stake. Other members include Pilipino Telephone Co, PT Pasifik Nusantara, Cable Entertainment Corp, Philippine Satellite Corp and China Everbright Group Ltd.</p>
